course: dictionary
lesson: 8094
title: A fish that hitches a ride
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A remora is a fish with a flat sucker on top of its head. «Remoras stick to sharks and rays with a sucker on their heads, and that sucker is really a changed fin.» The clue is in the words: a sucker is something that holds on tight.
explain: The remora uses its sucker to stick to sharks, whales, turtles and boats, and ride along with them. It gets a free ride and scraps of food, so it moves around without much effort.
explain: Scientists call animals that live together like this symbiosis. When one animal gains and the other is not harmed, the relationship is called commensalism. The remora is a good example of both words.
fact: A remora is a fish. The plural is remoras.
fact: The flat sucker on a remora's head is really a changed fin.
fact: Remoras stick to sharks, whales, turtles and boats.
fact: A remora on a shark is sometimes called a suckerfish.
fact: Remoras get a free ride and scraps of food from the animals they stick to.
exercise: «Remoras stick to sharks and rays with a sucker on their heads.» What is a remora? | A type of boat | A bird that lives near the sea | A shark that is very small | *A fish that rides along on bigger animals
exercise: What is the flat part on top of a remora's head used for? | To hear sounds in the sea | To catch flying insects | To swim faster through the water | *To stick to other animals and boats
exercise: A remora gets a free ride when it sticks to a shark. What else does it get? | Warm water to swim in | A new fin | *Scraps of food | Sharp teeth to bite with
test: «The sucker on a remora's head is really a changed fin.» What is the sucker really? | A bone | A tooth | *A changed fin | A tail
test: What is the scientific word for animals living together, like a remora and a shark? | Migration | *Symbiosis | Hibernation | Camouflage
exam: Which sentence is true? | *Remoras stick to sharks, whales and boats | Remoras eat only plants | Remoras are sharks | Remoras have no sucker
